# Legal review notes with explicit redline-style guidance.
output = ARGV.len() > 0 ? ARGV[0] : "markdown-review-notes.docx"; let body = """---
title: Vendor Agreement Review Notes
author: Imani Reed
subject: Counsel review checklist
theme: legal
page_numbers: true
---
# Vendor Agreement Review Notes

Prepared for **Cedar Valley Cooperative** on June 21, 2026.

## Priority changes

- Clarify the service credit cap in Section 4.
- Add a five-business-day notice period before suspension.
- Confirm that customer data is deleted after termination.

## Open questions

| Section | Question | Owner |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 4.2 | Does the credit apply to recurring fees? | Finance |
| 7.1 | Which subcontractors may access data? | Security |
| 9.3 | Is the renewal notice bilateral? | Legal |

## Counsel note

> Keep the indemnity language aligned with the cooperative’s approved fallback. Do not accept an uncapped obligation without executive review.

{{clause: 1}} Proposed fallback. Limit direct damages to fees paid in the prior twelve months, excluding confidentiality and data-security breaches.

{{sign: Imani Reed}}
""";
p=_lmcode_ cli="lmoffice docx" install="github:lmctl-ai/lmoffice@latest";
let d=docx.create(${output}); d.markdown(${body}).save();
end _lmcode_
savedsl(p,output+".dslb"); r=system(concat(dsl_cli(p),["--dsl",output+".dslb"]),120000); assert(r.code==0);
